{"kind":"finding","id":"F-ledger-career-023-01","file":"Source/Parsek.Tests/KerbalsWindowUITests.cs","line":684,"method":"MissionOutcomesAndRosterUseSameSubitemIndent","category":"T3","severity":"Low","confidence":"high","falsifiability":"falsifiability: Source/Parsek/UI/KerbalsWindowUI.cs:606; FormatRosterChainMemberText indent six spaces instead of SubitemIndent -> still green (StartsWith(SubitemIndent) is true and the length equality at KerbalsWindowUITests.cs:712-713 only measures outcomeText); make it three spaces -> red","what_it_asserts":"Both tabs' subitem helpers start with the shared four-space SubitemIndent constant (outcomeText exactly, rosterText as prefix) and outcomeText's indent length equals SubitemIndent.Length.","why_weak":"The roster side is only prefix-checked, so any LONGER roster indent passes; the length equality never reads rosterText. A widened roster indent leaves the two tabs misaligned while the parity guard stays green.","proposed_action":"Pin the roster indent exactly: assert rosterText.Substring(0, SubitemIndent.Length) == SubitemIndent and rosterText.Length minus the branch glyph plus FormatChainMember(member) equals SubitemIndent.Length, or compare both helpers' measured indent lengths.","effort":"S","july_ref":"none"}
